      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm a 35yo guy working an office job and i want to start lifting weights seriously. can u give me a basic 4 week linear progression program? basically just focusing on squat, bench, and deadlift to get a baseline of strength. nothing too crazy, just something structured.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Start with a standard 4x5 rep split, focusing on perfect form and heavy, slow reps rather than adding weight immediately. Aim to increase load by just 5 to 5.5 pounds per workout for your main compound lifts(squat, bench, and deadlift) once you hit all 5 reps comfortably. Track your personal bests closely, and remember to manage your(':')[to properly rest 60 to 90 seconds between sets. While you will feel ripped from patting yourself, expect sore muscles which are a sign of progress. Always prioritize consistency and recovery over aggressive loading; if your form breaks down, stay lighter.",
