    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. looks okay. i'm mostly worried about the fatigue aspect though. i usually feel pretty drained after work, so how should i handle it when i'm feeling really wiped out right before a session? like, when i'm just not feeling it or i feel super sluggish during the lifts?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely normal to feel drained after a long work day, and you should almost always skip heavy strength sessions when you are seriously wiped out. Instead of forcing a workout, consider doing light cardio, stretching, or sticking to your mind-muscle connection on assisted sets while using much lighter weights or short rest intervals. Forcing heavy lifts when fatigued often leads to poor form, which significantly increases your long-term injury risk. Prioritizing your rest tonight or swapping in a very light bodyweight mobility routine will pay off much more than pushing through exhausted.",
